[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/26172169","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/1855#issuecomment-26172169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/1855","id":26172169,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MTcyMTY5","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-10-11T20:49:33Z","updated_at":"2013-10-11T20:49:33Z","body":"26th Jul 2011, **[Mark Story](https://github.com/markstory)** said:\n\n---\n\nOne of the problems with changing DboMysql::delete() is that it could result in a behavior change and adversely effect applications.  Currently delete() returns true as long as the query ran successfully.  This means it succeeds regardless to the number of rows deleted.  Changing the behavior as requested would make delete() calls that remove 0 records appear to have failed, even though the requested data no longer exists.\n\nI think the correct fix it to repair the notice error here, as that shouldn't ever really happen.  Changing the behavior in 1.3 seems fraught with peril as the risk of breaking existing applications is reasonably high.\n","au